N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): onsets of the whole clip folded onto the cycle that repeats best (2.50 s): two strong strokes in it, 1.25 s apart, with weaker beats between, so a beat of about 0.62 s with every second one stressed. The pitch tracker found many voices at once and no single line; the pitches drift about 50 cents over the minute.
N:TRIED (2026-11-11): the singing was tracked again on the sustained part alone (drum, claps and wind taken out), and each pair of beats was matched to major and minor triads; the strongest line and the chords both moved by a semitone or more every few seconds, which is the pitch drifting as the camera passes different singers and the group goes flat, not a progression. Nothing reliable enough to write.
N:UNCERTAIN: the metre (two or four beats to the bar); which voice carries the tune; everything about the harmony.
